propagate the contents of the Program.

  In the following three sections, a "patent license" is any express
agreement or commitment, however denominated, not to enforce a patent
(such as an express permission to practice a patent or not to
enforce a patent as a covenant not to sue for patent infringement or
not to settle a patent dispute).  To "grant" such a patent license
means to make such an agreement or commitment not to enforce a patent.

  If you convey a covered work, knowing that it relies on a patent
license, and the corresponding source of the work is not available
for anyone to copy, free of charge and under the terms of this License,
through a public server or other readily accessible means, then you
must either (1) cause the corresponding source to be so available,
or (2) arrange to deprive yourself of the benefit of the patent
license for this particular work, or (3) extend the patent license
in the usual manner to anyone who acquires the covered work.  If you
